   College Python Courses},
Booktitle = {PROCEEDINGS OF THE 26TH ACM ANNUAL CONFERENCE ON CYBERSECURITY \&
   INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY EDUCATION, ACM SIGCITE 2025},
Year = {2025},
Pages = {324-325},
Note = {26th Annual Conference on Information Technology Education-SIGITE,
   Consumnes River College, Sacramento, CA, NOV 06-08, 2025},
Organization = {Jones \& Bartlett Learning LLC},
Abstract = {Community college students often face unique challenges in introductory
   programming {[}1], particularly first-generation andworking learners who
   balance coursework with jobs and family responsibilities {[}3]. To
   address these challenges, we piloted PyTutor, an MIT-developed
   LLM-powered tutoring system, in CSC101: Introduction to Python at
   Quinsigamond Community College. Surveys and grade comparisons between
   Fall 2024 (no PyTutor) and Spring 2025 (with PyTutor) reveal
   improvements in student confidence, positive perceptions, and modest
   grade gains. These results highlight the promise of AI tutors for
   scalable and equitable support in community college computing education.},
