   (SIGCSE TS), Toronto, CANADA, MAR 15-18, 2023},
Organization = {Assoc Comp Machinery; ACM Special Interest Grp Comp Sci Educ},
Abstract = {Due to the Covid-19 pandemic, most university classes were moved to
   online instruction. This greatly stimulated the need for online learning
   tools. WeBWorK is an open source online homework system, which has been
   used extensively in a variety of subjects. However, it has not been
   widely adopted by the Computer Science education community. In this
   paper, we discuss our experience using WeBWorK in teaching two large
   online sections of discrete mathematics. Emphasis is given to how we
   created randomized and auto-graded problems for many topics. In
   addition, we summarize student performance and feedback. We conclude
   with our reflections on using WeBWorK and propose future work for
   exploring its adaptive learning features.},
