   (AIED), Chicago, IL, JUN 25-29, 2019},
Abstract = {Hour of Code activities became a de facto standard for the first
   encounter with programming, reaching millions of children every year.
   These activities are typically not personalized and offer the same
   sequence of tasks to everybody, which leads to too slow pace for some
   students, while too fast for others. We aim to improve upon the current
   state of the art in teaching introductory programming by providing
   insight into how adaptive learning techniques can make the Hour of Code
   activities more efficient and engaging.},
