   Mendix; Springer; Univ Aberdeen; Aberdeen City Council},
Abstract = {Software development companies want new hires with strong interpersonal
   and problem solving skills. To ensure the development of such skills,
   they must be embedded throughout the curriculum. However, many students
   struggle to collaborate with peers and in self-regulated practice during
   the early stages of their course. Explicit scaffolding can, however,
   motivate such engagement. This tips and techniques session shows how an
   ice-breaker using LEGO EV3 robots at two UK institutions enhanced peer
   interaction and increased self-regulated practice over the first four
   weeks of 2016-17 and 2017-18.},
